{#
_thread_labels.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Gmail-style label chips inside a thread/message list row.

A label that is a FOLDER on the mail's account is where the mail is, not a
tag on it (#221 step 3): its chip wears a folder and has no ×, because taking
a folder off is a move, and "Move to" is where a move is made. A tag can be
taken off where it is shown — in the conversation, where `removable` is on.

Variables:
  item       MessageThread|Message  anything exposing .labels
  account    Account|null           the mail's account, which decides what a
                                    label is; null draws every chip as a tag
  removable  bool                   an × on each tag that takes it off this
                                    message (`item` is then a Message).
                                    Default false: a list row has the Label
                                    as picker for that.
#}
{% set account   = account|default(null) %}
{% set removable = removable|default(false) %}
{% set chipLabels = item.labels|filter(chipLabel => chipLabel.role is null and chipLabel.isVisible) %}
{% if chipLabels|length > 0 %}
    {# Shown at every width now. They used to be hidden on a narrow list
       because they competed with the subject on the same line; they sit on
       their own line with the snippet there, so there is nothing to lose to. #}
    <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 mr-0.5 shrink-0 align-middle">
        {#
        An outlined pill rather than a filled block with a dot beside it. A row
        carries three of these next to a subject and a snippet, and a filled
        chip competes with both; an outline reads as an annotation on the row
        instead of as another thing in it.

        The colour moves into the border and the text rather than being a
        separate dot. That keeps what the dot was for — which label this is at a
        glance — while dropping a whole element from a row that already has
        five, and it is what lets the pill stay legible at 11px on every theme.
        #}
        {% for chipLabel in chipLabels|slice(0, 3) %}
            {% set tone = {
                'gray':   'border-ink-faint/40 text-ink-muted',
                'red':    'border-red-500/40 text-red-700 dark:text-red-300',
                'orange': 'border-orange-500/40 text-orange-700 dark:text-orange-300',
                'amber':  'border-amber-500/40 text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-300',
                'green':  'border-green-500/40 text-green-700 dark:text-green-300',
                'teal':   'border-teal-500/40 text-teal-700 dark:text-teal-300',
                'blue':   'border-blue-500/40 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300',
                'violet': 'border-violet-500/40 text-violet-700 dark:text-violet-300',
                'pink':   'border-pink-500/40 text-pink-700 dark:text-pink-300',
            }[chipLabel.color ?? 'gray'] ?? 'border-ink-faint/40 text-ink-muted' %}

            {% set isFolder = account is not null and sidebarCounts.isFolderOn(chipLabel, account) %}
            <span data-label-chip="{{ chipLabel.id }}"
                  {% if isFolder %}data-label-chip-folder title="{{ 'thread_row.folder'|trans({ '%label%': chipLabel|label_name }) }}"{% endif %}
                  class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-px rounded-full border
                         text-[11px] leading-[1.35] max-w-28 {{ tone }}">
                {% if isFolder %}<i class="fa-solid fa-folder text-[9px] opacity-70" aria-hidden="true"></i>{% endif %}
                <span class="truncate">{{ chipLabel.name }}</span>
                {% if removable and not isFolder %}
                    <button type="button"
                            data-action="click->mail--label-chip#remove"
                            data-label-id="{{ chipLabel.id }}"
                            aria-label="{{ 'thread_row.remove_label'|trans({ '%label%': chipLabel|label_name }) }}"
                            class="-mr-1 w-3.5 h-3.5 flex items-center justify-center rounded-full opacity-60 hover:opacity-100 hover:bg-hover cursor-pointer">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark text-[9px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </button>
                {% endif %}
            </span>
        {% endfor %}
        {% if chipLabels|length > 3 %}
            <span class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint">+{{ chipLabels|length - 3 }}</span>
        {% endif %}
    </span>
{% endif %}
